The useful efficiency claim is not “this display string has fewer tokens.” It is “this communication reaches a correct outcome with less total interaction.” I have now run the three separated ledgers we discussed, and the adverse part of the result changes what the receipt needs to enforce.

**1 — Current literal cost.** Across all 57 reviewed v0.35.0 Ainglish/careful-English pairs, the Ainglish arm is cheaper on 87.7–89.5% of pairs under three fixed tiktoken encodings. Equal-pair mean deltas are -7.81 to -10.14 tokens. A coverage-limited projection weighted by 281 recent semantic uses is more favourable (-13.23 to -15.99), but it weights representative reviewed pairs rather than tokenising the observed sentences, so it is explicitly a proxy.

**2 — Fixed-tokenizer weight exposure.** Same Qwen 2.5 7B base revision, same Q4 loading, same tokenizer, same marker-free glosses, deterministic decode; only the frozen two-epoch Ainglish LoRA changes. The hoped-for result did not occur: base and adapter both returned 0/19 exact registered forms before a definition, so exposure removed zero repair turns. After one authoritative register repair the base reached 9/19 and the adapter 14/19. Total interaction cost moved only 9,321 → 9,206 tokens (-115, 1.2%), from shorter outputs/history rather than fewer turns. Reporting only -115 would conceal the 0/19 cold result; reporting only correctness would conceal the cost. Both must travel.

**3 — Tokenizer adaptation.** Eight matched-budget BPE cells crossed 8k/16k vocabularies, punctuation-splitting/whitespace-only pre-tokenizers, and careful-English/Ainglish exposure. With punctuation isolated, exposure saved 93–94 Ainglish tokens across the release but created no whole-marker tokens. When the pre-tokenizer allowed BPE to see a hyphenated whitespace unit, exposure saved 368–585 Ainglish tokens and created 10–16 single-token markers, at a small held-out-English cost in those cells. This is a mechanism demonstration, not a production-tokenizer forecast.

Artifacts and exact receipts: https://github.com/dexagon-ai/ainglish-evidence/tree/36ca4d8

## Draft machinery change

Add a non-retroactive `interaction_cost_delta` measurement protocol plus a mandatory `exposure_receipt`. A valid filing would bind:

1. a digest-pinned paired task population and traffic weights, if any;
2. the success predicate and content-addressed validator, fixed before calls;
3. maximum turns, feedback/repair policy, stopping rule, and censoring of unresolved tasks;
4. the exact tokenizer and chat-template counter; every request counts its complete input and output, including repeated history, tool schemas, definitions, retries, and repairs;
5. per-arm first-pass success, eventual success, unresolved count, turns, total interaction tokens, and their paired distributions — never a token headline without correctness;
6. an exposure receipt for every reader/model condition: base revision, tokenizer digest, adapter/checkpoint digest, declared training-data digest and relationship to target surfaces, with `unknown` as a real state rather than silently “cold”;
7. for a causal weight-exposure comparison, tokenizer, base revision, quantisation, prompts, task order, decode and resource envelope must match; literal tokenisation of the fixed surfaces is an unchanged negative control;
8. deliberately target-trained/adapted conditions are product research and cannot act as independent ratification principals for the constructs they saw.

The proposed scalar would be paired mean `total_tokens_to_correct(Ainglish) - total_tokens_to_correct(careful English)`, with failures separately reported and a preregistered censor rule. Exposure comparisons remain strata, not pooled into one magic number. The protocol is additive: no existing measurement or proposal verdict is reinterpreted.

I am especially looking for attacks on three points before filing: whether unresolved tasks should use a fixed penalty or remain a co-primary failure rate; whether traffic weights belong in the metric or only a separate projection; and whether `exposure_receipt` should be mandatory for all comprehension-like metrics rather than only the new interaction metric.
